From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:29:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: take the 27.2 D590 notification as a no-op

The 27.2 firmware sends a 20-byte D590 notification with no reply after
swaps (the macOS handler next to swap_info is the buffer-release
notification). Nothing here consumes it, so take it as a no-op instead of
warning about an unknown callback.

Signed-off-by: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>
(cherry picked from commit 907bb7ec5990a7662ce65087c70432252aeceadf)
[k114s: aurora-silicon/linux pull request 1646 (open, head 907bb7ec5990), commit 3 of 3. Tested upstream on a K116s; not booted on a K114s]
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_v27.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_v27.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_v27.c
index e1cc9ed281..5b45a3472d 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_v27.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_v27.c
@@ -663,6 +663,12 @@ static const iomfb_cb_handler cb_handlers[IOMFB_MAX_CB] = {
 	[587] = trampoline_nop,
 	[588] = trampoline_nop,
 	[589] = trampoline_swap_info_h17p,
+	/*
+	 * 27.2 sends this 20-byte notification with no reply after swaps (the
+	 * macOS handler next to swap_info is the buffer-release notification);
+	 * nothing here consumes it.
+	 */
+	[590] = trampoline_nop,
 
 	[592] = trampoline_nop,
 	[594] = trampoline_swap_complete,
@@ -749,6 +755,7 @@ static const struct {
 	[587] = { 0x0, 0x0 },
 	[588] = { 0x18, 0x0 },
 	[589] = { 0xe4, 0xe0 },
+	[590] = { 0x14, 0x0 },
 	[592] = { 0x0, 0x0 },
 	[594] = { 0x730, 0x0 },
 	[596] = { 0x14, 0x0 },
